# Dropped into /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/, so Debian's own defaults still apply and this file
# says only what differs. Read it as the list of decisions, not as a whole configuration.

# Both authentication methods are on, because B9 has to be measured against each: a password
# typed into a dialog, and a key that never prompts at all.
PasswordAuthentication yes
PubkeyAuthentication yes

# Nobody connects as root. Acter connects as a user with a home directory and a `.bashrc`,
# which is the case that has anything to teach us.
PermitRootLogin no

# Nothing here needs a display or a tunnel, and a test rig that offers them is a test rig
# with more attack surface than reason.
X11Forwarding no
AllowTcpForwarding no
AllowAgentForwarding no

# **`AcceptEnv` is deliberately left at the stock default, which accepts almost nothing.**
#
# This is the most important line in the file, and it is the one that is not here.
#
# B5.3's bash injection reaches the far end as an environment variable — `PROMPT_COMMAND`,
# carried across the WSL boundary by `WSLENV`. Over SSH there is no such carrier: a client
# may only send variables the *server* has agreed to accept, and OpenSSH's default agrees to
# `LANG` and `LC_*` and nothing else. A server belonging to somebody else will not have been
# configured for us.
#
# So a rig that added `AcceptEnv PROMPT_COMMAND` would let B9 ship an injection that works
# against this container and against nothing a user actually connects to. That is B4.5's
# lesson exactly — "should" is not evidence — and the honest rig is the restrictive one.
#
# **This measurement is what settled decision 2**: an SSH session is unintegrated. The line
# stays absent permanently, not pending a workaround. A later entry offers to install an
# integration snippet on the far end with the user's consent, and that entry is measured
# here too — against a server that accepts nothing, which is the server people have.

# Keep the greeting out of the byte stream: a banner would arrive before the shell says
# anything and would be indistinguishable from output to everything above the transport.
PrintMotd no
Banner none
